      "id": "claim_226677a055614def8b18a0857023e1f4",
      "statement": "Core search normalization is independent of the exported `filter_results()` utility: search uses private `_clean_result()` to discard falsey title/href, collapse title/body whitespace, decode DuckDuckGo redirects, and HTTPS-prefix non-HTTP(S) hrefs, whereas `filter_results()` only selects caller-supplied records with a minimum stripped title length and already HTTP(S)-prefixed href, preserving accepted title/href values and defaulting a missing body to an empty string.",
